How many DISTINCT boundary functions does one stretch have, over all interior placements?
                       chain   resolution   distinct boundary functions
                  +97 *3 +13   round-to-8                             1
                  +97 *3 +13     identity                             1
                   *3 >>1 *5   round-to-8                             4
                   *3 >>1 *5     identity                             1
              +97 *5 >>1 +13   round-to-8                             3
              +97 *5 >>1 +13     identity                             2
                   *3 *3 +97   round-to-8                             3
                   *3 *3 +97     identity                             1

C-A  identity resolution gives exactly 1 distinct boundary function on every chain: False   (must be True)
C-B  a fully-bound stretch has 1 placement by construction, so 1 function: True
C-C  chains where the free schedule yields more than one boundary function: 3 of 4   (must be > 0)
C-D  inputs whose BOUNDARY output differs between two placements: 0 of 256   (must be > 0)

VERDICT
  On a stretch with a free interior adaptation point, 'the stretch's boundary
  function' is a definite description with no unique referent: the stretch has
  up to 4 of them. Clause 2 licenses realisations that induce THE boundary
  function; clause 3 places the schedule choice under clause 2; and the schedule
  choice is exactly what selects among them.
